@*
    OdsPopupMenu: ONE real <button> trigger with a popover anchored to it (issue #255). It is the
    shared host behind every select-style Ods control (OdsMultiSelect, OdsSortSelect, OdsTypeSelect,
    OdsPageSizeSelect, OdsInlineSelect, OdsTagMultiSelect, OdsMoneyField's currency picker,
    AccountSmartTagAdder, CreateTransactionDialog's account picker).

    Why it exists: MudMenu wraps a custom ActivatorContent in its own
    <div tabindex="0" role="button" aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="…">. Every Ods trigger put a
    real <button> inside that div, which gave each control two tab stops (an unnamed "button", then
    the real one), announced a button nested in a button, and left aria-expanded on the div rather
    than on the focused, named control.

    It is built on MudPopover + MudOverlay directly rather than MudMenu, because MudMenu also
    hard-codes role="menu" on its list — wrong for a checkbox panel or a search-plus-listbox, and
    impossible to override. Here the panel's role follows what it holds, and the trigger's
    aria-haspopup always agrees with it:
      • single-choice mode (RowId/RowCount set): role="menu" of the consumer's
        role="menuitemradio" rows; aria-haspopup="menu";
      • panel mode (everything else — a checkbox group, a search box, a listbox): a non-modal
        role="dialog" named by the trigger; aria-haspopup="dialog".

    MudPopover positions against the parent of its placeholder, which is this component's box, so
    the popover anchors, flips and portals out of any overflow:hidden ancestor as before; MudOverlay
    closes it on an outside click, as MudMenu's did.

    Keyboard (APG menu button / disclosure dialog):
      • Enter/Space (the button's own click), ↓ or ↑ on the trigger open it, and focus moves IN:
        the selected row (single-choice), FocusOnOpenId, or else the panel's first focusable;
      • single-choice rows rove with ↑/↓/Home/End (clamped) and Tab closes behind itself;
      • Esc anywhere in the panel, or on the trigger while open, closes and returns focus to the
        trigger. While open the trigger stops its keys propagating, so that Esc does not also
        cancel a wrapping OdsModal; closed, keys bubble as normal;
      • a close by outside click also hands focus back to the trigger rather than <body>.
*@

@inject IJSRuntime Js

<div class="@WrapperClass" @attributes="UserAttributes">
    @BeforeTrigger
    <button @ref="_trigger"
            type="button"
            id="@EffectiveTriggerId"
            class="@TriggerClassName"
            disabled="@Disabled"
            aria-haspopup="@HasPopup"
            aria-expanded="@(_open ? "true" : "false")"
            aria-controls="@(_open ? PanelId : null)"
            aria-label="@AriaLabel"
            aria-describedby="@AriaDescribedBy"
            aria-invalid="@(AriaInvalid ? "true" : null)"
            @onclick="OnTriggerClickAsync"
            @onkeydown="OnTriggerKeyDownAsync"
            @onkeydown:stopPropagation="@_open">
        @TriggerContent
    </button>
    <MudPopover Open="@_open"
                Class="@PopoverClass"
                AnchorOrigin="@AnchorOrigin"
                TransformOrigin="@TransformOrigin"
                RelativeWidth="@RelativeWidth"
                MaxHeight="@MaxHeight">
        <div id="@PanelId"
             class="@PanelClassName"
             role="@(SingleChoice ? "menu" : "dialog")"
             aria-labelledby="@(string.IsNullOrEmpty(AriaLabel) ? EffectiveTriggerId : null)"
             aria-label="@AriaLabel"
             @onkeydown="OnPanelKeyDownAsync">
            @ChildContent
        </div>
    </MudPopover>
    <MudOverlay Visible="@_open" AutoClose="true" LockScroll="false" OnClosed="OnOverlayClosedAsync" />
</div>
